  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile this change ensures `is_static_input_scheme` is a boolean, the code will actually crash at line 699 if `input_quant` is `None`. The helper method `_is_dynamic_token_w4a8_int` (and others like `_is_static_tensor_w8a8` at line 685 and `_is_dynamic_token_w8a8` at line 692) does not handle `None` for the `input_quant` argument and will raise an `AttributeError` when accessing `input_quant.num_bits` or `input_quant.strategy`. To properly support weight-only schemes where `input_activations` is `None`, these helper methods must be updated to include `None` checks.",
      "created_at": "2026-05-20T20:57:55Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -697,7 +697,7 @@ def _get_scheme_from_parts(\n                 )\n \n             if self._is_dynamic_token_w4a8_int(weight_quant, input_quant):\n-                is_static_input_scheme = input_quant and not input_quant.dynamic\n+                is_static_input_scheme = bool(input_quant and not input_quant.dynamic)",
